{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> The reason for <b>the God of Israel.</b> Because those who worshipped it thought that it was idolatry:" "<b>And let each man kill his brother.</b> Even if he is his brother. And many interpreted 'the one who says to his father and to his mother' (Deuteronomy 33:9) as referring to this deed, and they were forced to explain 'his father and his mother' as the mother's father. But there is no need, as I will explain in its place:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:52.175207249Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}